    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-x/q6",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-x/q6-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The mass of a radioactive isotope decays at a rate proportional to the mass of the isotope present. The half life of the isotope is 80 years. Determine the percentage of the original amount which remains after 50 years. ( 11 )\" style=\"--madas-width:593.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-x/q6-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Let m be the mass after t years and M the initial mass: Decay at a rate proportional to the mass gives dm/dt = −km, with k &gt; 0. [M1] Separating gives dm/m = −k dt. [M1] Integration gives ln m = −kt + C since the mass is positive: [M1] Exponentiating gives m = eCe−kt = Ae−kt . [A1] At t = 0, m = M, so A = M. [A1] The half-life condition is M/2 = Me−80k, [A1] hence e80k = 2. [A1] The handwritten solution takes eighth roots to obtain e10k = 21/8. [A1] Taking logs also gives k = (ln 2)/80 ≃0.00866434, and 21/8 ≃1.09051. At t = 50, m = Me−50k = M(e10k)−5, [A1] hence m = M2−5/8. [A1] The percentage remaining is\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-x/q6-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"100m/M = 100 2−5/8 ≈64.8% . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 6 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The mass of a radioactive isotope decays at a rate proportional to the mass of the isotope present. The half life of the isotope is 80 years. Determine the percentage of the original amount which remains after 50 years. ( 11 )"
